### Point of Sale — end-to-end walkthrough (VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio .http)
@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Browse the catalog (seeded on first start)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/products?search=latte

### 2. Create a product (Inventory opens a stock record via RabbitMQ)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "COF-MOC-001",
  "name": "Mocha",
  "category": "Coffee",
  "price": 4.25,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 3. Receive stock for a product (replace with a real product id)
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/inventory/{{productId}}/receive
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 50 }

### 4. Ring up a sale -> 202 Accepted, status Pending
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cashierId": "till-01",
  "items": [ { "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 2 } ]
}

### 5. Poll the order until status = AwaitingPayment
@orderId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### 6. Pay with a Stripe test card (confirmed server-side)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{orderId}}/intent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentMethodId": "pm_card_visa" }

### 6b. Or simulate a decline, then retry step 6
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{orderId}}/intent
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentMethodId": "pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined" }

### 7. Order is now Paid and stock committed
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/inventory/{{productId}}

### Cancel an unpaid order (releases reserved stock, voids the PaymentIntent)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Customer left" }
